# Deliberately NO `ignore-scripts=true` — see docs/09 §7.
#
# pnpm >= 10 already blocks dependency lifecycle scripts by default and
# requires an explicit `pnpm.onlyBuiltDependencies` allowlist in package.json.
# That is a strictly better version of what ignore-scripts bought us: the
# allowlist is reviewable, per-package, and committed. Setting ignore-scripts
# on top of it is worse than redundant — it also suppresses the allowlist, so
# esbuild never links its native binary and `pnpm build` cannot run at all
# (found in spike S1, 2026-07-27).
